{{-- Breadcrumb trail. Reads a `crumbs` array from the including page's server
    block — @include does not accept inline data in this version (an
    `['crumbs' => …]` argument leaves the variable undefined and the loop
    reports "crumbs is not iterable"), and the page needs the array declared
    anyway to drive its @structuredData BreadcrumbList from the same source.

    Each crumb is { label, href?, url? }. The last has no href: it is the
    current page.

    Deliberately NOT the shipped Breadcrumb component. That component builds its
    trail with @foreach(item in displayItems), and the loop parser only accepts
    the ` as ` form — the ` in ` form is skipped outright, so the literal
    directive text would ship to the browser on all 22 pages.

    Ordered list, not a row of anchors: this is a sequence, the position is
    meaningful, and assistive tech should say so. The separators are decorative
    and hidden from it; the current page is marked aria-current.

    StxLink rather than a bare anchor. It compiles to `<a href data-stx-link>`,
    and the SPA router only intercepts elements carrying that attribute — a
    plain `<a href="/projects">` does a native full page reload instead. This
    was the last internal link in the app still doing that. Where a full load
    IS wanted (the OAuth redirects in login/register), the anchor stays plain
    and says so with data-no-router. --}}
<nav class="shell subnav" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <ol>
    @foreach (crumbs as c)
      <li>
        @if ($loop.last)
          <span aria-current="page">{{ c.label }}</span>
        @else
          <StxLink to="{{ c.href }}">{{ c.label }}</StxLink><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        @endif
      </li>
    @endforeach
  </ol>
</nav>
